From: Protium
Subject: [PATCH] wsi/metal, kk: Say how presents reached the screen (KK_PRESENT_STATS)

A FIFO game can sit at 20 fps with 38 ms of every frame in
vkAcquireNextImageKHR (DOOM 2016), and nothing says whether the GPU is slow
or the compositor holds the drawables. With KK_PRESENT_STATS=<seconds> the
driver writes one line to stderr every so many seconds of presents:

  MESA: info: KosmicKrisp: presents of the last 30 s (<program>, <HH:MM:SS>):
  presents, how many were paced and at which rate, shown, not shown, let go
  by Metal and without a drawable; the time from the present call to
  presentedTime and how much of it came after the GPU had finished the
  command buffer that presents the drawable; how many refreshes apart the
  shown presents were; the wait in acquire and nextDrawable's own time; the
  GPU's busy time (the union of the command buffers' GPUStartTime to
  GPUEndTime); the most presents the compositor held at once; swapchains
  made and destroyed; whether the window was hidden.

A swapchain that is destroyed writes the line of its last seconds, when there
is at least one second of them. Unset, the statistics cost one atomic read a
present and a command buffer.

